::ALG2_U03_L02_GP01::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_GP01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
What is the domain of f(x) = sqrt(x - 7)?
{
=A. x >\= 7#Correct. The radicand x - 7 must be nonnegative.
~B. x <\= 7#That would make many radicands negative.
~C. all real numbers#Square root functions require a nonnegative radicand.
~D. y >\= 7#Domain describes x-values, not y-values.
}

::ALG2_U03_L02_GP02::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_GP02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
What is the range of g(x) = sqrt(x) + 4?
{
~A. x >\= 4#This confuses domain and range.
=B. y >\= 4#Correct. The parent range y >= 0 shifts up 4.
~C. y <\= 4#The graph starts at 4 and increases.
~D. all real numbers#A square root graph does not have all real y-values.
}

::ALG2_U03_L02_GP03::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_GP03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
What is the endpoint of h(x) = sqrt(x + 2) - 5?
{
~A. (2, -5)#The sign inside the radical is reversed.
~B. (-5, -2)#The coordinates are reversed.
=C. (-2, -5)#Correct. The graph shifts left 2 and down 5.
~D. (2, 5)#Both shifts have incorrect signs.
}

::ALG2_U03_L02_GP04::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_GP04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
Which function is the parent square root function shifted right 3 units?
{
~A. f(x) \= sqrt(x + 3)#Adding inside shifts left, not right.
~B. f(x) \= sqrt(x) + 3#Adding outside shifts up.
~C. f(x) \= sqrt(x) - 3#Subtracting outside shifts down.
=D. f(x) \= sqrt(x - 3)#Correct. Subtracting inside shifts right 3.
}

::ALG2_U03_L02_GP05::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_GP05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
What is the domain of f(x) = cuberoot(x + 1)?
{
=A. all real numbers#Correct. Cube root functions accept negative, zero, and positive radicands.
~B. x >\= -1#That restriction applies to square roots, not cube roots.
~C. x <\= -1#Cube roots are defined on both sides of -1.
~D. y >\= 0#This describes a range restriction, not the domain.
}

